  'Read the actual load current: close the clamp meter jaws around a single conductor, never around two phases, and read the AC amperage without breaking the circuit.' => '读取实际负载电流：将钳形表钳口夹住单根导线（绝不能夹在两根相线上），无需断开电路即可读取 AC 电流值。',
  'Read the outside air temperature and compare it with the system design load' => '读取室外空气温度，并与系统设计负荷比较',
  'Recommended Instruments' => '推荐仪器',
  'Record indoor and fridge temperatures to catch a failing thermostat' => '记录室内和冰箱温度，捕捉温控器失效',
  'Reliable everyday measurement for the wiring checks most workshop calls start with.' => '可靠、日常的测量，适用于大多数维修车间上门服务开始时进行的线路检查。',
  'Replace any lead with cracked or damaged insulation before you use it again.' => '表笔绝缘层出现裂纹或损坏时，在再次使用前应更换。',
  'Run continuity checks: switch to continuity or buzzer mode, short the leads to confirm the tone, then test the conductor end to end and compare the reading with the circuit length.' => '进行导通检查：切换到导通或蜂鸣模式，将表笔短接确认有提示音，然后对导体进行端到端测试，并将读数与电路长度比较。',
  'Safely re-energise the circuit, then check the LED driver DC output across its output terminals while the lamp is connected, keeping the capacitor-discharge caution in mind.' => '安全地重新为电路通电，然后在灯具连接的情况下测量 LED 驱动输出端子两端的 DC 输出，同时牢记电容放电的注意事项。',
  'Safety First' => '安全第一',
  'Safety First on Live Circuits' => '带电电路，安全第一',
  'Safety First: Household Electrical Work' => '安全第一：家庭电气作业',
  'Set the BT-168 Series for the cell type and read the load-tested verdict, or switch to DC voltage mode and compare open-circuit voltage with the rating stamped on the battery.' => '将 BT-168 系列设为相应的电池类型，读取带载测试结论；或切换到 DC 电压模式，将开路电压与电池上标注的额定值比较。',
  'Set the meter to DC voltage mode and read the battery at the terminals with the engine off. A healthy 12V battery rests near 12.6V and a 24V system near 25.2V.' => '将仪表设为 DC 电压模式，在发动机关闭时于端子处读取电池电压。健康的 12V 电池静置电压约为 12.6V，24V 系统约为 25.2V。',
  'Socket Tester Outlet Receptacle Tester' => '插座测试仪（插座插孔检测仪）',
  'Stand on a dry insulating mat and keep the meter and leads clear of moisture.' => '站在干燥的绝缘垫上，并保持仪表和表笔远离潮湿。',
  'Surface temperature readings flag an overloading motor, bearing or fuse before it fails.' => '表面温度读数能在电机、轴承或熔断器失效前提示过载。',
  'Switch to DC voltage mode and probe from ground to each point along the circuit with the load switched on. A drop above about 0.5V between battery and load points to a corroded terminal or thin wire.' => '切换到 DC 电压模式，在负载接通时从接地端沿电路逐点测量。电池与负载之间超过约 0.5V 的压降，表明存在腐蚀的端子或过细的导线。',
  'Test for voltage on a machine isolator before opening the cover' => '打开机盖前，在机器隔离开关上测试是否有电压',
  'Test the charging system: with the engine running, read battery voltage at the terminals at idle and again at a higher rpm — a healthy alternator lifts the reading into its working range and holds it steady.' => '测试充电系统：在发动机运转时，分别于怠速和较高转速下读取端子处的电池电压——健康的发电机应使读数上升到其工作范围内并保持稳定。',
  'Test the meter before any live work: select AC voltage mode, confirm it reads the local supply on a known-good outlet, then touch the probes together to verify the continuity buzzer sounds.' => '在任何带电作业前先测试仪表：选择 AC 电压模式，确认仪表在已知正常的插座上能读到当地供电电压，然后将表笔碰在一起，确认导通蜂鸣器鸣响。',
  'Test the meter first. In AC voltage mode, prove the tester on a known live source, and re-prove it on the same source when you finish so a failed meter can never give a false safe reading.' => '先测试仪表。在 AC 电压模式下，用已知带电的电源验证测试仪，完工后在同一电源上再次验证，这样即使仪表失效也绝不会给出虚假的安全读数。',
  'Test the meter first. Plug the leads into the correct sockets, set the rotary switch to AC voltage mode, and confirm a known-good outlet reads mains voltage.' => '先测试仪表。将表笔插入正确的插孔，把旋转开关转到 AC 电压模式，并确认在已知正常的插座上能读到市电电压。',
  'Test the meter first: confirm the DC voltage reading on a known-good battery, then short the leads in continuity mode to hear the buzzer before working on the vehicle.' => '先测试仪表：在一节已知正常的电池上确认 DC 电压读数，然后在导通模式下将表笔短接以听到蜂鸣声，之后再在车辆上作业。',
  'Test the meter first: set it to AC voltage mode and confirm it reads the expected supply value on a known-good live source before you trust any reading.' => '先测试仪表：将其设为 AC 电压模式，在已知正常的带电电源上确认它能读到预期的供电值，然后再信任任何读数。',
  'Test the meter first: touch the probe tips together in continuity mode and confirm the buzzer sounds, then verify AC voltage mode against a known live outlet.' => '先测试仪表：在导通模式下将表笔尖端碰在一起，确认蜂鸣器鸣响，然后用已知带电的插座验证 AC 电压模式。',
  'Test the meter on a known live source again after the job, so a meter that failed mid-check can never be missed.' => '作业结束后，再在已知带电的电源上测试一次仪表，这样仪表在检查中途失效也绝不会被漏掉。',
  'These meters cover the everyday checks above without the bulk and cost of a full lab bench.' => '这些仪表即可覆盖上述日常检查，无需整套实验室台架的体积和成本。',
  'These tools cover the everyday checks above with the least fuss and the lowest risk on a household call-out.' => '这些工具即可覆盖上述日常检查，家庭上门服务时最省事、风险最低。',
  'This scenario covers the temperature, voltage and current checks you run when servicing refrigeration, heating and air conditioning equipment.' => '本场景涵盖维护制冷、供暖和空调设备时执行的温度、电压和电流检查。',
  'To chase a 12V circuit that sags, stay in DC voltage mode, energise the load, and watch for the voltage drop that betrays a corroded terminal or undersized cable.' => '排查电压下降的 12V 电路时，保持 DC 电压模式，接通负载，并留意会暴露腐蚀端子或线径不足电缆的电压降。',
  'To check a winding, fuse or breaker, de-energise the circuit first and use continuity or buzzer mode to confirm a near-zero reading.' => '检查绕组、熔断器或断路器时，先切断电路电源，再用导通或蜂鸣模式确认读数接近零。',
  'To check running current on a compressor or fan motor, clamp the jaws around a single conductor in AC current mode, never around a cable carrying both live and neutral.' => '检查压缩机或风机电机的运行电流时，在 AC 电流模式下将钳口夹住单根导线，绝不能夹在同时承载火线和零线的电缆上。',
  'To test a heating element, switch to resistance mode, de-energise the circuit, and measure across the element, expecting a low continuous resistance rather than an open circuit.' => '测试加热元件时，切换到电阻模式，切断电路电源，测量元件两端的电阻，应得到较低的连续电阻，而非开路。',
  'Trace a 12V car circuit that drops voltage when the load switches on' => '排查在负载接通时电压下降的 12V 汽车电路',
  'Trace a heating element that cycles off before the room reaches set point' => '排查在室温到达设定值之前就循环关断的加热元件',
  'Trace a lamp that stays dark by testing the switch in both positions' => '通过测试开关的两个位置，排查一直不亮的灯具',
  'Trace a live feed inside a distribution board without breaking the circuit' => '无需断开电路，排查配电箱内的带电进线',
  'Track live and dead wires quickly on 12V and 24V car circuits.' => '在 12V 和 24V 汽车电路上快速区分带电与不带电的导线。',
  'Tracks indoor temperature and humidity to flag a drifting thermostat or a damp room.' => '监测室内温度和湿度，以提示温控器漂移或房间潮湿。',
  'Treat every 12V or 24V wire as live until you prove otherwise — vehicle circuits can push serious current.' => '在证实之前，应把每根 12V 或 24V 导线都当作带电处理——汽车电路可能产生很大的电流。',
  'Use its clamp jaws to compare current across the phases of a three-phase motor and spot imbalance.' => '使用其钳形夹口比较三相电机各相之间的电流，发现不平衡。',
  'VC3270 / VC3269 Digital Clamp Meters' => 'VC3270 / VC3269 数字钳形表',
  'VC3270 Digital Clamp Meter' => 'VC3270 数字钳形表',
  'Verify a breaker is carrying an overload before it trips' => '在断路器跳闸前，确认其是否承受过载',
  'Verify correct live-neutral-earthing polarity at every household socket' => '在每个家用插座处验证火线—零线—接地极性是否正确',
  'Verify refrigerant pipe surface temperatures when the compressor runs weak' => '当压缩机运转无力时，验证制冷剂管道的表面温度',
  'Verify the supply voltage at the appliance inlet is actually present' => '验证电器进线处确实存在供电电压',
  'Voltage checks are safe when the right habits are automatic. These rules apply whether you work on a factory floor or a domestic board.' => '当正确的习惯成为本能时，电压检查就是安全的。无论你在车间还是在家庭配电箱作业，这些规则都适用。',
  'Voltage, current and a stored capacitor can hurt long after the switch is off. Keep these habits in front of you every time you pick up the meter.' => '电压、电流和储存的电容在开关关闭很久之后仍可能造成伤害。每次拿起仪表时，都要牢记这些习惯。',
  'What to Measure in Electrical Maintenance' => '电气维护中的测量内容',
  'What to Measure in HVAC and Temperature' => 'HVAC 与温度中的测量内容',
  'What to Measure in Home Electrical Checks' => '家庭电气检查中的测量内容',
  'What to Measure in Industrial Maintenance' => '工业维护中的测量内容',
  'What to Measure in LED and Appliance Repair' => 'LED 与电器维修中的测量内容',
  'What to Measure on a Vehicle' => '车辆上的测量内容',
  'Wilk 302 / 303 Car Electric Pens' => 'Wilk 302 / 303 汽车测电笔',
  'Work from the battery outward and always compare each live reading against a known-good reference. A steady sequence gives you readings you can trust and repeat.' => '从电池开始向外排查，始终将每个带电读数与已知正常的参考值比较。稳定有序的操作能给你可信且可重复的读数。',
  'XT101 Temperature Meter' => 'XT101 温度计',
  'XT2017 Digital Clamp Meter' => 'XT2017 数字钳形表',
  'XT300 Temperature Meters' => 'XT300 温度计',
  'XT802' => 'XT802',
  'check continuity on a dead 12V circuit before tracing the fault' => '在排查故障前，检查已断电 12V 电路的导通性',
  'check continuity on a dead 230V outlet before calling it failed' => '在判定 230V 插座故障之前，先检查其导通性',
  'check for a lost neutral by comparing hot to neutral and hot to earth' => '通过比较火线—零线和火线—地线，检查是否零线丢失',
  'check voltage drop across a corroded earth strap or battery terminal' => '检查腐蚀的接地带或电池端子两端的电压降',
  'confirm the absence of voltage before opening a breaker panel' => '打开断路器面板前，确认无电压',
  'confirm which pin stays live on a 12V or 24V wiring harness' => '确认 12V 或 24V 线束上哪个针脚保持带电',
  'measure battery resting voltage to spot a weak or undercharged cell' => '测量电池静置电压，以发现老化或充电不足的电芯',
  'measure live-to-earth voltage to spot a high-leakage neutral' => '测量火线—地线电压，以发现漏电大的零线',
  'test a tripped breaker to see whether the fault sits in the load' => '测试跳闸的断路器，判断故障是否出在负载侧',
  'test alternator output with the engine idling and again under rev' => '在发动机怠速和升速状态下测试发电机输出',
  'trace a 12V car circuit that drops voltage under load' => '排查带载时电压下降的 12V 汽车电路',
  'trace a car circuit that drops voltage under load when lights are on' => '排查开灯时带载电压下降的汽车电路',
  'verify fuse and relay continuity after a component stops working' => '在某个部件停止工作后，验证熔断器和继电器的导通性',
  'verify line and neutral polarity at a socket outlet before energising' => '在通电前，验证插座处的火线和零线极性',
);
